meta {
  name: Outstanding Summary Grouped
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/outstanding-summary/grouped?statuses=ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED&groupBy=outsource
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  statuses: ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED
  groupBy: outsource
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
  ~branchId: {{branchId}}
  ~search: john
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Grouped Outstanding aggregate powering the dimension panels — the due>0 view of
  `/orders/billing-summary/grouped` (same shared grouping layer with
  `report:'outstanding'`). `groupBy` = the SAME set as Billing (b2b / ref-by /
  internal-referral / external-referral / int-ref-user / ext-ref-user / lab-test /
  lab-panel / department / category / subcategory) **plus `outsource`**.

  - `outsource` groups by the **outsource center** (`OutsourceCenter.name`) of the
    order's accession `SampleTransfer` (`kind=OUTSOURCE`) — the /accession/outsource
    dataset, re-sourced like internal/external referral (each order attributed to
    its primary transfer's center).
  - `internal-referral` / `external-referral` group by accession-transfer
    destination; `int-ref-user` / `ext-ref-user` by the order's referral user;
    `lab-test` / `lab-panel` by test/panel code; `department` / `category` /
    `subcategory` by classification (branch scalar ?? master catalogue).

  Every row is order-level money over the due>0 dataset, so `Σ grouped` reconciles
  with `/orders/outstanding-summary` and `/orders/outstanding-records`.
}
